			"Message": "test(Rest): Add comprehensive test suite for OXC compiler\n\nThis commit introduces a complete testing infrastructure for the Rest compiler's OXC implementation, ensuring reliability and VSCode compatibility.\n\n## New Test Files\n\n### Unit Tests (`tests/unit/oxc_compiler.rs`)\n- Parser tests: verify TypeScript parsing with correct AST generation\n- Transformer tests: validate AST transformation with TypeScript/JSX support\n- Codegen tests: ensure valid JavaScript output generation\n- Decorator tests: verify legacy decorator handling matches VSCode behavior\n- Source map tests: confirm proper source map generation\n- Config derivation tests: validate parser/transformer configs from CompilerConfig\n- Performance benchmarks: measure compilation speed for medium-sized files\n\n### Integration Tests (`tests/integration/vscode_compatibility.rs`)\n- VSCode compatibility comparison tests for out/ and out-build/ directories\n- File-by-file comparison with mismatch reporting\n- TypeScript file discovery and filtering (.d.ts and test file exclusion)\n- VSCode compatibility benchmarks (ignored, requires VSCode source)\n- VSCode vs Rest performance comparison benchmarks\n\n### Test Library (`tests/lib.rs`)\n- Central module re-exporting compiler components for tests\n- Re-exports OXC::Compiler, CompilerConfig, SWC types\n\n## Dependencies Added\n- Added `tempfile` and `walkdir` workspace dependencies for test file handling\n\n## Module Re-exports\n- Exported OXC::Compiler from Source/Fn/mod.rs for testing\n- Exported CompilerConfig, ModuleFormat, BuildOption, CommandOption from Source/Struct/mod.rs\n\nThis test suite validates the OXC migration from recent commits, ensuring the compiler produces output compatible with VSCode's build pipeline for the Cocoon extension host.",
			"SHA": "1e2f4081903fa1428c82f7b021c4b47716f79724"
		},
